course: dictionary
lesson: 8730
title: Words about giant trees
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sequoia is a huge evergreen tree from California. Evergreen means it keeps its green leaves all year. You can use the word for one tree or for many: a sequoia, two sequoias.
explain: Read the words around it to get the meaning. «The General Sherman tree in California is the biggest single tree by volume; sequoias live for thousands of years.» Biggest, thousands of years and fire-proof bark all tell you a sequoia is a giant, very old tree.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in: «Sequoias live for thousands of years» works if a sequoia is a tree that lives a very long time. If your meaning makes the sentence strange, look again at the clues.
fact: A sequoia is a huge evergreen tree from California.
fact: There are two kinds: the giant sequoia and the coast redwood.
fact: «General Sherman» is a giant sequoia and is the biggest single tree by volume.
fact: Coast redwoods are the tallest trees; «Hyperion» is about 116 metres tall.
fact: Sequoias have thick bark that helps them survive forest fires, and some cones only open after fire.
exercise: «A giant sequoia called General Sherman is so wide that a family car could park across its trunk.» What is a sequoia? | A kind of fast-moving bird | A small flower that grows in gardens | *A huge evergreen tree from California | A type of rock
exercise: «Their thick bark helps them survive forest fires.» What does the thick bark help a sequoia do? | Run faster | Grow new leaves in winter | *Survive forest fires | Swim across rivers
exercise: Which two kinds of sequoia are named in the dictionary? | *Giant sequoia and coast redwood | Ash and birch | Oak and pine | Cherry and apple
test: Which tree in the sentences is the biggest by volume? | Hyperion | Sequoyah | *General Sherman | Coast redwood
test: The word sequoia is named after whom? | An Australian writer | *Sequoyah, a Cherokee man who made a writing system | A Californian farmer | A Scottish king
exam: Why can a sequoia survive a forest fire? | Its leaves are made of metal | Its roots are made of stone | *Its thick bark helps protect it | It lives under water
